---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';
import { breadcrumbList } from '@/lib/breadcrumbs';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Terms', href: '/terms/' },
];

const jsonLd = [breadcrumbList(crumbs)];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use for FeeCalc Payment Calculators"
  description={`Terms of use for ${siteConfig.siteName} fee calculators: educational estimates only, not financial advice. Always verify live provider rates before pricing decisions.`}
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
  modified="2026-11-07"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: 2026-11-07</em></p>
  <p class="answer-first">
    By using {siteConfig.siteName}, you agree that calculators are educational estimates only — not financial, tax, or
    legal advice — and that you will verify fees on each provider’s official site before making decisions.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to the public website, embeddable calculator snippets, and related pages (guides, hubs, examples,
    methodology, changelog). If you do not agree, do not use the site. Continued use after we post updates constitutes
    acceptance of the revised terms; the “Last updated” date above is the effective date.
  </p>

  <h2>License</h2>
  <p>
    You may use the calculators for personal or internal business planning. You may embed widgets if you keep the credit
    link back to {siteConfig.siteName}. You may not scrape the site to build a competing thin copy, misrepresent
    affiliation with payment brands (Stripe, PayPal, Square, Venmo, Cash App, Patreon, Ko-fi, Gumroad, Shopify, Zelle,
    Wise, or others named on tool pages), remove attribution from embeds, or use the service for unlawful activity.
  </p>

  <h2>No financial advice</h2>
  <p>
    Outputs are estimates from published list rates with last-verified dates. Providers may offer custom or negotiated
    pricing, promotions, or region-specific schedules that differ from public pages. Currency conversion, chargebacks,
    instant-transfer fees, platform commissions, and tax are often separate from the card-processing line item. Nothing
    on this site is a recommendation to choose a particular processor or to pass fees to customers.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranties</h2>
  <p>
    Fee schedules change without notice. We provide data “as is” and “as available,” with methodology and source links,
    but no warranty of completeness, accuracy, merchantability, or fitness for a particular purpose. Automated rate
    watching and manual checks reduce staleness; they do not guarantee a match to your live merchant dashboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {siteConfig.siteName} and its maintainer are not liable for lost profits,
    pricing mistakes, missed payouts, chargebacks, tax outcomes, or other damages arising from reliance on calculator
    outputs or site content. Your sole remedy for dissatisfaction is to stop using the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Calculator amounts are processed in your browser. Analytics and advertising cookies (if enabled) follow the rules in
    our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, including AdSense disclosures and consent defaults. Do not submit
    sensitive payment-card numbers or government IDs through the contact form.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party brands</h2>
  <p>
    Product names and logos belong to their owners. References are for identification and fee-education only. This site
    is independent and is not endorsed by those brands unless a page explicitly says otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> or{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
